                                               \u2502\n\u2502  The `aws-s3-vault-storage` project has been fully implemented according to  \u2502\n\u2502  the modular architecture design.                                            \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### Project Structure                                                       \u2502\n\u2502  - `providers.tf`: Global provider configuration.                            \u2502\n\u2502  - `variables.tf`: Root input variables.                                     \u2502\n\u2502  - `outputs.tf`: Root outputs.                                               \u2502\n\u2502  - `main.tf`: Root module call.                                              \u2502\n\u2502  - `README.md`: Project documentation.                                       \u2502\n\u2502  - `modules/storage/`:                                                       \u2502\n\u2502      - `main.tf`: Resources for S3, versioning, and lifecycle.               \u2502\n\u2502      - `variables.tf`: Module-specific variables.                            \u2502\n\u2502      - `outputs.tf`: Module-specific outputs.                                \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  All files were created successfully using the `Write Terraform File` tool.  \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2570\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256f\n\n\u256d\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 \ud83d\udccb Task Completion \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256e\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Task Completed                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Name: Based on the Architect's modular design, implement the Terraform      \u2502\n\u2502  project: aws-s3-vault-storage.                                              \u2502\n\u2502  --- ARCHITECTURE DESIGN ---                                                 \u2502\n\u2502  PROJECT_SLUG: aws-s3-vault-storage                                          \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 1. Provider and Resource Identification                                 \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Provider:** `hashicorp/aws`                                           \u2502\n\u2502  *   **Resources:**                                                          \u2502\n\u2502      *   `aws_s3_bucket`: For storage (`test-vault-storage`).                \u2502\n\u2502      *   `aws_s3_bucket_versioning`: To enable versioning.                   \u2502\n\u2502      *   `aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration`: To define the 30-day       \u2502\n\u2502  transition rule to Glacier.                                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 2. Modular Architecture Layout                                          \u2502\n\u2502  ```text                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502  .                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.tf                 # Root module calls storage module              \u2502\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500\u2500 providers.tf            # Provider configuration                        \u2502\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500\u2500 modules/                                                                \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 storage/                                                            \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 main.tf         # S3 bucket, versioning, and lifecycle          \u2502\n\u2502  resources                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 variables.tf    # Bucket name, lifecycle days                   \u2502\n\u2502  \u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 outputs.tf      # Bucket ARN/ID                                 \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 3. Implementation Details                                               \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  **providers.tf**                                                            \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  terraform {                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502    required_providers {                                                      \u2502\n\u2502      aws = {                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502        source  = \"hashicorp/aws\"                                             \u2502\n\u2502        version = \"~> 5.0\"                                                    \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  provider \"aws\" {                                                            \u2502\n\u2502    region = \"us-east-1\"                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  **modules/storage/main.tf**                                                 \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"vault\" {                                          \u2502\n\u2502    bucket = var.bucket_name                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"aws_s3_bucket_versioning\" \"vault_versioning\" {                    \u2502\n\u2502    bucket = aws_s3_bucket.vault.id                                           \u2502\n\u2502    versioning_configuration {                                                \u2502\n\u2502      status = \"Enabled\"                                                      \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  resource \"aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration\" \"vault_lifecycle\" {        \u2502\n\u2502    bucket = aws_s3_bucket.vault.id                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502    rule {                                                                    \u2502\n\u2502      id     = \"transition-to-glacier\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502      status = \"Enabled\"                                                      \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502      transition {                                                            \u2502\n\u2502        days          = 30                                                    \u2502\n\u2502        storage_class = \"GLACIER\"                                             \u2502\n\u2502      }                                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  **main.tf**                                                                 \u2502\n\u2502  ```hcl                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  module \"s3_storage\" {                                                       \u2502\n\u2502    source      = \"./modules/storage\"                                         \u2502\n\u2502    bucket_name = \"test-vault-storage\"                                        \u2502\n\u2502  }                                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ### 4. Architecture Diagram                                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ```mermaid                                                                  \u2502\n\u2502  graph TD                                                                    \u2502\n\u2502      subgraph Root                                                           \u2502\n\u2502          M[main.tf]                                                          \u2502\n\u2502      end                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502      subgraph modules/storage                                                \u2502\n\u2502          S3[aws_s3_bucket: test-vault-storage]                               \u2502\n\u2502          VER[aws_s3_bucket_versioning]                                       \u2502\n\u2502          LIFE[aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration]                         \u2502\n\u2502      end                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502      M --> S3                                                                \u2502\n\u2502      S3 --> VER                                                              \u2502\n\u2502      S3 --> LIFE                                                             \u2502\n\u2502  ```                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502  ---------------------------                                                 \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## MANDATORY RULES (FAILURE TO FOLLOW = BROKEN CODE)                        \u2502\n\u2502  1. You MUST use the `Write Terraform File` tool for EVERY SINGLE FILE you   \u2502\n\u2502  create.                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502  2. DO NOT WRITE PLAIN TEXT TERRAFORM. YOU MUST CALL THE TOOL.               \u2502\n\u2502  3. If you need to create 15 files, you MUST call the tool 15 times.         \u2502\n\u2502  4. If a \"PREVIOUS ROUND FAILED\" block is present, you MUST prioritize       \u2502\n\u2502  correcting the reported errors and applying the provided KNOWN FIX          \u2502\n\u2502  GUIDANCE or reflection advice. You MUST override the Architect design if    \u2502\n\u2502  it contradicts the required fix (e.g. if the design specifies               \u2502\n\u2502  \"enable_auto_scaling = true\" but the guidance instructs to rename it to     \u2502\n\u2502  \"auto_scaling_enabled = true\", you MUST apply the rename).                  \u2502\n\u2502  5. STRICT MODULAR STRUCTURE REQUIREMENT:                                    \u2502\n\u2502     You MUST organize the code into logical submodules under the `modules/`  \u2502\n\u2502  directory (e.g., `./modules/networking`, `./modules/aks`,                   \u2502\n\u2502  `./modules/acr`).                                                           \u2502\n\u2502     The root `main.tf` must only call these modules. You MUST use the        \u2502\n\u2502  `Write Terraform File` tool to create `main.tf`, `variables.tf`, and        \u2502\n\u2502  `outputs.tf` for EACH module, as well as the root files.                    \u2502\n\u2502     DO NOT write all resources flatly in the root directory.                 \u2502\n\u2502  6. You MUST create a `README.md` in the project ROOT.                       \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## HCL FORMATTING (CRITICAL)                                                \u2502\n\u2502  - NEVER use semicolons (;) to separate arguments. Use NEWLINES.             \u2502\n\u2502  - Every resource argument MUST be on its own line.                          \u2502\n\u2502  - Every closing brace } MUST be on its own line.                            \u2502\n\u2502  - BAD:  resource \"aws_subnet\" \"s1\" { vpc_id = aws_vpc.main.id; cidr_block   \u2502\n\u2502  = \"10.0.1.0/24\" }                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  - GOOD:                                                                     \u2502\n\u2502    resource \"aws_subnet\" \"s1\" {                                              \u2502\n\u2502      vpc_id     = aws_vpc.main.id                                            \u2502\n\u2502      cidr_block = \"10.0.1.0/24\"                                              \u2502\n\u2502    }                                                                         \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## REQUIRED FILES                                                           \u2502\n\u2502  - Root files: Define the `terraform { required_providers { } }` block and   \u2502\n\u2502  `provider` block exactly once in `versions.tf` or root `main.tf`. DO NOT    \u2502\n\u2502  duplicate provider blocks in submodules.                                    \u2502\n\u2502  - Root `variables.tf`: Input variables (e.g., region).                      \u2502\n\u2502  - Root `outputs.tf`: Key outputs (endpoints, IDs, ARNs).                    \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  ## EKS / INFRASTRUCTURE COMPLETENESS CHECKLIST                              \u2502\n\u2502  If creating EKS, you MUST include ALL of the following:                     \u2502\n\u2502  - At least 2 subnets across 2 different Availability Zones (EKS requires    \u2502\n\u2502  this).                                                                      \u2502\n\u2502  - Subnets must have `map_public_ip_on_launch = true` for public clusters.   \u2502\n\u2502  - IAM roles MUST have `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` resources:           \u2502\n\u2502    * Cluster role: AmazonEKSClusterPolicy                                    \u2502\n\u2502    * Node role: AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy,                                   \u2502\n\u2502  AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly, AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy                    \u2502\n\u2502  - EKS `vpc_config` must include `endpoint_public_access = true` for public  \u2502\n\u2502  clusters.                                                                   \u2502\n\u2502  - Node group must have `depends_on` referencing the IAM policy              \u2502\n\u2502  attachments.                                                                \u2502\n\u2502  - Subnets should be tagged: `kubernetes.io/cluster/<name> = shared`.        \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502  Project Slug: aws-s3-vault-storage                                          \u2502\n\u2502  Agent: Senior Terraform Developer                                           \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2502                                                                              \u2502\n\u2570\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u256f\n\n\u256d\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25